  "tagline": "Ochre, clay, moss, and bark — the natural pigments of Japanese craft.",
  "description": "Earth tones run through the full range of Japanese material culture: the iron-oxide browns of ceramics, the umber of aged lacquer, the mossy greens of forest paths, the warm greys of stone lanterns. Traditional Japanese color names capture all of them, not as backdrop neutrals but as protagonists. These palettes are practical for interior design, residential branding, organic food and beverage, and any identity rooted in the natural world.",
